---
// UseCases — three columns showing where Codec wins, framed by who's
// at each end of the wire. Pulled from the cross-stack matrix in
// packages/bench/results/2026-05-08T01-15-02Z/MATRIX.md.
//
// The dict-zstd numbers (354 B at 2 K tokens on sglang) are model-to-model
// territory — humans never see the bytes, the dict is pre-shared once,
// and msgpack frames compress to a control byte and a delta.
---

<section id="use-cases" class="section usecases">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">where Codec wins</p>
    <h2>One wire format. Three traffic classes. <span class="usecases__title-mute">Different math each time.</span></h2>
    <p class="usecases__lede">
      Codec moves token IDs, not text. Whoever's on either end &mdash; user,
      model, agent, tool &mdash; the bytes are the same shape. But the
      <em>amount</em> of byte savings depends on who's talking to whom.
    </p>

    <div class="usecases__grid">
      <article class="uc">
        <header class="uc__head">
          <span class="uc__tag">human &rarr; model</span>
          <h3>The chat path</h3>
        </header>
        <p class="uc__body">
          Someone types a question. The user's prompt and the model's reply
          are both wire-native &mdash; no UTF-8 round-trips on either end.
          The reply stream is where the bytes actually flow on a chat UI: a
          short chat-length reply shrinks <strong>~67&times;</strong> on the
          wire (15.2 KB JSON-SSE &rarr; 226 B Codec+gzip on sglang at 64
          tokens), and longer answers scale up to <strong>1,404&times;</strong>
          at 2&nbsp;K tokens. TTFB stays within 1&nbsp;ms of plain JSON-SSE
          on the same server &mdash; faster paint on flaky networks, no
          latency tax.
        </p>
        <ul class="uc__metrics">
          <li><span class="uc__num">67&times;</span><span>short chat reply</span></li>
          <li><span class="uc__num">0</span><span>UTF-8 round-trips</span></li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="uc uc--m2m">
        <header class="uc__head">
          <span class="uc__tag uc__tag--accent">model &rarr; model</span>
          <h3>The agent backbone</h3>
        </header>
        <p class="uc__body">
          One model hands off context to another. No human eyes on the wire,
          no JSON for human readers to parse. The vocabulary is fixed at
          handshake, the dict is pre-shared, and msgpack frames collapse to
          a control byte plus a delta. <strong>1,404&times;</strong> at 2&nbsp;K
          tokens on sglang &mdash; <strong>237 B/token down to 0.17 B/token</strong>.
          This is the lane Codec was built for.
        </p>
        <ul class="uc__metrics">
          <li><span class="uc__num">1,404&times;</span><span>at 2 K tokens</span></li>
          <li><span class="uc__num">354 B</span><span>per 2 K-token reply</span></li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="uc">
        <header class="uc__head">
          <span class="uc__tag">model &rarr; tool</span>
          <h3>The tool-call boundary</h3>
        </header>
        <p class="uc__body">
          The model emits a reserved control ID; the runtime sees it as a
          single 32-bit compare per token instead of detokenizing back to
          UTF-8 and regex-matching <code>&lt;tool_call&gt;</code>.
          <strong>100&times; faster</strong> at 1&nbsp;M tokens on the
          ToolWatcher microbench &mdash; sub-millisecond turnaround on every
          single tool boundary, in-band with the stream.
        </p>
        <ul class="uc__metrics">
          <li><span class="uc__num">100&times;</span><span>vs detokenize+regex</span></li>
          <li><span class="uc__num">0.61 ms</span><span>per 1 M tokens</span></li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .usecases__title-mute { color: var(--fg-faint); font-weight: 500; }
  .usecases__lede { max-width: 64ch; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .usecases__lede em { color: var(--fg); font-style: normal; font-weight: 600; }

  .usecases__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
  @media (min-width: 880px) {
    .usecases__grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
  }

  .uc {
    background: var(--bg-elev);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .uc--m2m {
    /* model-to-model is the headline use case — give it the accent border */
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--data) 50%, var(--border));
    background:
      radial-gradient(120% 140% at 0% 0%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--data) 8%, transparent), transparent 65%),
      var(--bg-elev);
  }

  .uc__head { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .uc__tag {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-self: flex-start;
    padding: 0.125rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
    color: var(--fg-faint);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .uc__tag--accent {
    background: var(--data-soft);
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--data) 60%, transparent);
    color: var(--data);
  }
  .uc h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .uc__body {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .uc__body strong { color: var(--fg); font-weight: 600; }
  .uc__body code {
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 0.05rem 0.3rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 0.85em;
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  .uc__metrics {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: auto 0 0;
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 1rem;
  }
  .uc__metrics li {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.125rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    color: var(--fg-faint);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .uc__num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--data);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    text-transform: none;
  }
  .uc--m2m .uc__num { color: var(--control); }
</style>
